 "notes": [
  "THE BOUNTY BOARD -- the Attack tab's BOUNTIES body (client/scenes/attack/bounty_board.gd), cut from bounties.png (art/slices/bounties.json).",
  "Laid 74 units HIGHER than painted: bounties.png's tab rule stands at 427 and attack.png's at 353. arena.png's stands at 483, so the two bodies shift by different amounts -- the design pack's draft manifest had copied arena's tab rects into bounties' and was fifty units out.",
  "poster: the four WANTED sheets the board was painted with. A slot with no price on it shows the painting's own empty poster -- nothing is laid over it.",
  "amount: the three prices the SERVER prepares. The one chosen wears the gold; the others are dim ink. The client sends the plate's id and never a number, and the fee is printed as the server sent it.",
  "on_head_row / your_row: each band was painted with one empty row; more are drawn under it at the row's own height."
 ],
